# iceberg-schema-id-allocation-v15.patch
#
# Applies to: duckdb-iceberg @ 5edc45f0 (branch v1.5-variegata), DuckDB v1.5.x.
#
# A port of upstream duckdb-iceberg c1cfe2ef ("fix: Allocate new schema ids from
# the highest existing id instead of the current one", PR #1438, issue #1436),
# which is on main only: v1.5-variegata does not have it (checked up to
# 5dcf5070), nor does the duckdb-iceberg that DuckDB v1.5.5 ships (45163a28).
#
# Problem: every ALTER path copies the current schema and numbers the copy one
# above the current schema's id, and AddSchemaOrGetExisting reuses an existing
# schema equal to the new one, compared by field ids, names and types but not
# by schema id. A change that returns the table to an earlier schema, such as a
# DROP COLUMN of the column the last ADD COLUMN added, makes that earlier schema
# current again, and the next change computes an id a later schema already has:
# "Attempted to add schema with id N, but this already exists in the table!".
# An ADD COLUMN always takes a new field id, so it never equals an existing
# schema, and the table can take no new column; the Iceberg mirror runs inside
# the user's statement, so the hot-side change rolls back with it.
#
# Fix: IntroduceNewSchema numbers the new schema GetMaxSchemaId() + 1 (the
# table's loaded schema versions hold every schema in the metadata), the
# per-path increments are gone, RemoveColumn keeps the id for IntroduceNewSchema
# to set, and the two paths that registered the schema inline (RENAME COLUMN,
# SET DEFAULT) call IntroduceNewSchema. Upstream's SET_COLUMN_COMMENT path does
# not exist at this ref.
#
# ci/journey.sh's second add-and-drop cycle (TC-228) fails without this patch.
# Drop the patch when ICEBERG_REF moves to a ref that has the fix: git apply
# --check then fails on the removed lines.
#
